    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d413">

                <pb facs="0539" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5151/898: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-08T17:00:00+07:00">July 8, 1942—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 9—4:44 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>813. For Secretary of Treasury from Adler.</p>
                <p>TF–49. Board at meeting today, which chairman invited me to attend as observer,
                    decided to change its official rate for Chinese national currency to 5<hi
                        rendition="#superscript">1/16</hi> United States cents and 3<hi
                        rendition="#superscript">1/64</hi> pence to be effective <pb facs="0540"
                        n="530" xml:id="pg530"/> as from the opening of business July 10. Banks
                    selling rate will be 5 United States cents and 3 pence. [Adler.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
